routineStarters.description:
What an empty Routines page offers to ask Caw for: what the project
repeats or waits on, as routines (project-starters.ts), in that order;
none while Jev is off.

starters.description:
What an empty board and Caw's panel offer to say to him: written for the
project from what it holds now (project-starters.ts), in that order;
none while Jev is off.

memory.description:
The user-scope memory (CLAUDE.md). Absent from a daemon that predates it;
`failed` is how a machine says its own copy was edited and was not
overwritten.

message_id.description:
The id the harness stores the message being written under, where it
stores it while it is written (opencode): what {@link STREAM_SO_FAR}
names, so a stored copy of the same message is not drawn beside it.

CommandAck.description:
Hub → client, the command's lifecycle:
- `accepted` — validated, the target daemon reachable, dispatched;
- `applied`  — the daemon confirmed, where its protocol carries a
  confirmation today; where it does not, the hub stops at `accepted` and
  the stream event reflecting the change is the proof of application;
- `failed`   — terminal, with the reason a human can read.

summary.description:
What will happen and why, in one line: "Change the fleet's CLAUDE.md";
for a shell call, the session's own reason for it ("Check whether the
two commits are on origin/main"), its command under it in `command`.

StartersChangedFrame.description:
Hub-originated: a project's starters for one place were written again;
the whole set, in its order (empty when none is offered, Jev off
included).
